  "_svg_note": "The published .drawio.svg and .drawio.png are exported by hand from the .drawio in draw.io. Re-export whenever this spec changes.",
  "_intent": "How the components fit together after the HA hardening, not how they are configured. Sizes, counts and settings live in the LMS Infrastructure Specifications.",
  "_layout_notes": [
    "Symmetric two-column layout: ap-southeast-2a on the left, ap-southeast-2b on the right. Anything that spans both zones \u2014 the load balancer, the Auto Scaling group, the database subnet group \u2014 sits in the centre gap, straddling.",
    "Subnet labels carry both the scenario AZ and the Learner Lab AZ, so a student can match what the console shows them.",
    "Straddling boxes sit below each subnet's label band so they do not clip it.",
    "Straight lines beat routed ones. Align the centres of any two boxes an edge joins, so the renderer draws one segment rather than a dog-leg \u2014 a diagram reads far faster when the connectors are straight. Keep the whole thing tight enough to sit on one page."
  ],
  "_delta_from_start": "AT3 adds: private-app-b, an outbound path for it, application capacity in both zones, an RDS standby in private-data-b, and HA alarms. Everything else is unchanged from the post-cutover baseline.",
  "title": "YAT LMS - HA hardened (end of AT3)",
